,\\\"value\\\":39},\\\"guard\\\":null}],\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"interrupts\\\":[],\\\"notes\\\":[\\\"The tick 316 release check held; applied-load behavior is not yet established.\\\",\\\"Any test result applies only to its recorded force, duration, direction and actual materials.\\\",\\\"A failed test or untying refusal requires reassessment, not an assumption that the materials were recovered.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[\\\"Prefer small reversible practical experiments over unsupported strength claims.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"sectioned-cord-study\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can I make a continuous longer reed cord that fits my branch-crossing trial?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"At tick 309 the seven-round operation released a continuous two-ply cord with 0.5 m twisted length and 0.54 m overall length.\\\",\\\"At tick 316 this cord completed the right-angle crossing binding and passed its release check.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"Fit and release retention are demonstrated for these pieces only; strength and durability remain unestablished.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Make a longer continuous cord and establish whether it fits the actual crossing.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[\\\"Learned the sectioned method.\\\",\\\"Made the longer cord.\\\",\\\"Used it in a completed crossing binding.\\\"],\\\"outputs\\\":[\\\"item-303-wren-3473\\\",\\\"binding-313-wren-3568\\\"],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"No further work for the fit question; bounded load testing belongs to the binding study.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Retain the measured fit finding and inspect the cord after binding tests.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"The longer cord resolved the earlier measured length shortfall in an actual completed binding.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"crossing-binding-study\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a handmade reed cord reversibly bind my two actual branch pieces at a crossing?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"